     5	## Contract and evidence
     6	
     7	- **Claim:** classify local spectral degree-of-polarization invariance for all scalar probes of a finite-spatial-mode source; distinguish deterministic probes from arbitrary incoherent mixtures; give the corresponding observable far-zone spectral condition and counterexamples to implication.
     8	- **Baseline:** Wolf's sufficient far-zone condition; the factorized electromagnetic Gaussian Schell-model sufficient condition of Zhao et al. (2009); standard Bloch-ball/qubit-channel geometry (Ruskai, Szarek and Werner, 2002). See `STATUS.md` for exact scopes and citations.
     9	- **Missing ingredient for the book's full problem:** the set of scalar probes realizable by *only* free-space propagation is much smaller than all linear probes, and full Maxwell propagation is not scalar on polarization. Our necessary conditions for all probes are not necessary conditions for that smaller set.
